# HTML must always be LF. Vite's HTML transform preserves the source file's
# line endings, so a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf smudges these to CRLF
# and vite carries that CRLF into dist/ — which then fails the Linux dist-sync
# CI guard (#18, #22). eol=lf forces LF on checkout AND on staging, making
# CRLF-in-HTML impossible rather than merely detected.
*.html text eol=lf
